   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "### Reference image (details to take) - ON\nAny picture that shows the details you want - the image the mesh was made from, or concept art: letters, runes, symbols, ornaments, a book cover. FLUX gets it as **image 2** next to every tile of the mesh's own views and paints its details on - any mesh, no alignment. *Tile References* turns it upside down for the upside-down tiles, so letters stay readable.\n**No reference?** Select these nodes + the two '+/- reference' nodes, press Ctrl+B, and use this prompt:\n\nEnhance the surface detail of this flat-lit 3D asset render without changing it: sharpen edges and patterns and add fine, realistic micro-detail that suits each material, such as weave on fabric, grain on wood, pores on skin, strands in fur or hair, scratches on metal and texture on stone. Keep exactly the same colors, saturation, brightness, shapes, design and composition as the input image. Flat, even, shadowless lighting and the same plain background."
   ],
